      body: `Born in Eleusis of an aristocratic family. Fought at Marathon in 490 BCE and almost certainly at Salamis in 480. Lost his brother Cynegeirus at Marathon. By ancient testimony, the man who introduced the second actor to the tragic stage — the innovation that made genuine dramatic dialogue possible. Composed perhaps eighty plays, of which seven survive. Won the first prize at the Dionysia thirteen times. The Oresteia was performed in 458 BCE when he was about sixty-seven. It is the only complete tragic trilogy to survive from antiquity. He died at Gela in Sicily in 456 or 455.`,
